TITLE:: MapperUnits
summary:: a provider for effects that list their own parameters
categories:: Libraries>Mapper
related:: Classes/Mapper, Classes/MapperTarget

DESCRIPTION::
Holds things by name and makes each of their parameters a target,
code::[\units, name, key]::. A thing qualifies when its class answers code::mapParams:: - a list
of code::(key:, label:, kind:, spec:, section:):: - and it answers code::mapGet(key):: and
code::mapSet(key, value)::. Every effect built on sc-eq's FxUnit does.

With sc-eq installed, the master chain's eq:

code::
Mapper.units.put(\masterEq, \FxChain.asClass.master.eq);
Mapper.default.map(\m1, \kn_1_1, [\units, \masterEq, \gain3]);
Mapper.units.removeAt(\masterEq);
::

Anything else that holds effects - a mixer with inserts, a module with a chain per pad - is a
provider of its own and uses link::#*describe:: for the descriptions, so they read the same
everywhere. The provider does not own the units: freeing one is its owner's business, and a
freed one should be taken off with link::#-removeAt::.

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new

METHOD:: describe
One parameter of one unit as a target description.
ARGUMENT:: unit
the effect
ARGUMENT:: key
one of its map params
ARGUMENT:: name
what the unit is called in labels
ARGUMENT:: group
where it sits in the window's list
ARGUMENT:: path
the path the description carries
RETURNS:: an Event, or nil when the unit has no such parameter

METHOD:: describeAll
Every parameter of one unit.
ARGUMENT:: unit
the effect
ARGUMENT:: name
what it is called
ARGUMENT:: group
where it sits
ARGUMENT:: pathOf
a Function from a key to that parameter's path

